{"term":"violet","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:f58880f2f09a21d63c","definition":"A plant or flower of the genus Viola, especially the fragrant Viola odorata; (inexact) similar-looking plants and flowers.","example":"Refreshed by their cooling bath of evening dew, the violets and other nocturnal flowers emitted a pleasant fragrance over the fields, but from the bogs and the rivulets came up now and then damp, penetrating gusts, that sent an icy chill through me.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["rooster"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["extraviolet","nonviolet","starviolet","violaniline","violetear","violetish","violetlike","violetness","violetward","violetwood","violety"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:98c537e20281997941","definition":"A person thought to resemble V. odorata, especially in its beauty and delicacy.","example":"‘Tom,’ he said, ‘you are looking at a crushed violet, a spent egg, a squeezed tube.’","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fuchsia","indigo","magenta","purple","rose","thistle","ultraviolet","violet"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["extraviolet","nonviolet","starviolet","violaniline","violetear","violetish","violetlike","violetness","violetward","violetwood","violety"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:408ff151501d128522","definition":"The color of most violets; the colour evoked by the shortest visible wavelengths between 380 and 435 nm, an additive tertiary colour.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fuchsia","indigo","magenta","purple","rose","thistle","ultraviolet","violet"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily"